Licensing of the paper, the thesis and the PDFs
==============================================

The MIT License in the repository root (../LICENSE) applies to the software in
code/ only. It does not apply to anything described in this file.


1. Paper, thesis and PDFs: all rights reserved
----------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2025-2026 the authors. All rights reserved.

This covers:

  - the LaTeX sources, text, figures and tables under paper/pcsc/ and
    paper/thesis/;
  - the compiled PDFs GLPE-PCSC2026-paper.pdf and GLPE-thesis.pdf in the repository
    root;
  - earlier drafts and proposal material that exist only in the Git history of
    this repository (for example under paper_proposal/).

The one exception is the third-party material in section 2 and the templates
in section 3, which are not covered wherever they appear. That includes the
pages of that material that are embedded in GLPE-thesis.pdf (the thesis includes
the approval and declaration forms, the reviews, the certificate, the
proof-of-publication capture and a co-author's curriculum vitae as page
images).

You may read and cite this material. You may not republish, redistribute or
reuse it, in whole or in part, without the written permission of the authors.
The authors of each document are named in the document itself; the PCSC 2026
paper is also listed in ../CITATION.cff.


2. Third-party material stays with its owners
---------------------------------------------

Some documents under paper/thesis/sections/images/ were created by others and
are included only as supporting documents of the thesis. They are not licensed
by this repository, and no rights in them are granted here:

  - reviewers' comments (pcsc_reviews/);
  - certificates (pcsc_presentation_certificate/);
  - approval and declaration forms (thesis_approval/ and
    declaration_of_authorship_and_originality/);
  - the proof-of-publication capture (proof_of_publication/);
  - any institutional or publisher logos that appear on those pages;
  - the curriculum vitae of a co-author (curricula_vitae/).

Contact their owners for any reuse.


3. LaTeX templates keep their own terms
---------------------------------------

The files in paper/pcsc/templates/ are third-party. Each keeps its own licence
terms and header notices, and this repository does not relicense them:

  - pcsc/acmart.cls (ACM): the notice at the top of the file defers to the
    terms in acmart.dtx; the acmart package is distributed on CTAN under the
    LaTeX Project Public License (LPPL).
  - icml/icml2024.bst and iclr/iclr2024_conference.bst: LPPL, version 1 or any
    later version, as stated in their headers.
  - neurips/neurips_2023.sty, icml/icml2024.sty and
    iclr/iclr2024_conference.sty: the conference author kits. The files carry
    no licence notice; the rights remain with the conference or the original
    authors.
